<article class="env-lemma" id="0G8U">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0G8U">Lemma <span data-tag="0G8U">10.126.8</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $I \subset R$ be a nilpotent ideal. Let $S$ be an $R$-algebra such that $R/I \to S/IS$ is of finite type. Then $R \to S$ is of finite type. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose $s_1, \ldots , s_ n \in S$ whose images in $S/IS$ generate $S/IS$ as an algebra over $R/I$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/00DV" data-tag="00DV">10.20.1</a> part (11) we see that the $R$-algebra map $R[x_1, \ldots , x_ n] \to S$, $x_ i \mapsto s_ i$ is surjective and we conclude. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>